---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../../config/site";

const prose = "max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-stone-600";
const sectionHeading =
  "text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-stone-900 sm:text-3xl";
const linkAccent =
  "rounded font-medium text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-700 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-stone-900";

// Employment progression, shown as a compact record rather than repeating
// the role bullets that live on /experience/. Years are locked at year
// precision to match the Experience content collection.
const roles = [
  { title: "TechOps Engineer · YuviTal", years: "2023 - 2024" },
  { title: "TechOps Team Lead · YuviTal", years: "2024 - 2026" },
] as const;
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`About ${siteConfig.name} | Production & Reliability`}
  description="About Ido Hail: Technical Operations experience across production systems, data and reliability, plus hands-on infrastructure and DevOps projects."
>
  <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-stone-900 sm:text-5xl">
    About
  </h1>

  <div class="mt-6 space-y-4">
    <p class={prose}>
      My background is in Technical Operations: running production systems and
      staying close to what they are actually doing.
    </p>
    <p class={prose}>
      Much of that work starts as investigation. Reading the logs, querying the
      database, following data through a system until its behavior makes sense,
      then turning what I find into the monitoring, automation and validation
      that stop the same question coming back.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section aria-labelledby="background-heading" class="mt-16">
    <h2 id="background-heading" class={sectionHeading}>
      Professional background
    </h2>

    <ul class="mt-6 max-w-2xl space-y-3">
      {
        roles.map((role) => (
          <li class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-x-4 gap-y-1 border-t border-stone-200 pt-3">
            <span class="font-medium text-stone-900">{role.title}</span>
            <span class="text-sm text-stone-500">{role.years}</span>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>

    <div class="mt-6 space-y-4">
      <p class={prose}>
        I joined YuviTal as a TechOps Engineer, working hands-on across
        production and staging: backend and database testing, investigating
        production issues, and validating the data flows and integrations behind
        them.
      </p>
      <p class={prose}>
        Moving into the Team Lead role added ownership without moving me away
        from the systems. I led a three-person team, one developer and two
        TechOps engineers, and stayed directly involved in monitoring, release
        readiness, data-quality automation, access administration and internal
        tooling. The detailed record is on the <a
          href="/experience/"
          class={linkAccent}>experience</a
        > page.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="how-i-work-heading" class="mt-16">
    <h2 id="how-i-work-heading" class={sectionHeading}>How I work</h2>
    <div class="mt-6 space-y-4">
      <p class={prose}>
        I am hands-on by default and work from the evidence before deciding what
        the fix should be. I am curious, comfortable owning a problem nobody has
        pinned down yet, and used to translating technical constraints for the
        engineering, product, business, vendor and client stakeholders who do
        not live in them every day. I have mentored teammates while staying
        hands-on. I am also a former combat commander, an experience that taught
        me to stay composed under pressure.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="cloud-heading" class="mt-16">
    <h2 id="cloud-heading" class={sectionHeading}>
      Cloud, infrastructure and what is underneath
    </h2>
    <div class="mt-6 space-y-4">
      <p class={prose}>
        More recently, I have been building the cloud and infrastructure side
        through hands-on projects: AWS with Terraform, Kubernetes and
        containers, CI/CD and observability. The <a
          href="/projects/"
          class={linkAccent}>projects</a
        > on this site are where that work is demonstrated, and a 2026 DevSecOps program
        and earlier study at See Security College cover the same ground more formally.
        It all helps when a problem turns out to sit a layer lower than expected.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="outside-heading" class="mt-16">
    <h2 id="outside-heading" class={sectionHeading}>Outside the terminal</h2>
    <div class="mt-6 space-y-4">
      <p class={prose}>
        Outside work I spend time in the gym and, when I get the chance,
        underwater. Scuba diving is the one I would keep if I had to pick.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
